<edge source="Enapter AEM Electrolyser EL 4.0" target="UKCA mark">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The Enapter AEM Electrolyser EL 4.0 conforms to UKCA mark according to Supply Machinery (Safety) Regulations 2008.</data>
  <data key="d9">conforms_to</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-d9f905a36fae7e407107d1a11e7b7200</data>
  <data key="d11">Enapter_Datasheet_EL40_EN.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1792055472</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Enapter AEM Electrolyser EL 4.0" target="CSA/ANSI B22734:2023 Ed.1 Hydrogen Generators Using Water Electrolysis - Industrial, Commercial, and Residential Applications">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The Enapter AEM Electrolyser EL 4.0 conforms to CSA/ANSI B22734:2023 Ed.1 for hydrogen generators using water electrolysis in industrial, commercial, and residential applications.</data>
  <data key="d9">conforms_to</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-d9f905a36fae7e407107d1a11e7b7200</data>
  <data key="d11">Enapter_Datasheet_EL40_EN.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1792055472</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Enapter AEM Electrolyser EL 4.0 :: Production Rate" target="Enapter AEM Electrolyser EL 4.0 :: Nominal Power Consumption per Nm³ of H₂ Produced">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Production rate, nominal power consumption, operative power, water consumption, and heat dissipation together define the operating envelope of the Enapter AEM Electrolyser EL 4.0.</data>
  <data key="d9">related_to</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-d9f905a36fae7e407107d1a11e7b7200</data>
  <data key="d11">Enapter_Datasheet_EL40_EN.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1792055475</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Enapter AEM Electrolyser EL 4.0 :: Production Rate" target="Enapter AEM Electrolyser EL 4.0 :: Water Consumption">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Water consumption of ~420 mL/h is close to the stoichiometric requirement for 500 NL/h H₂ production.</data>
  <data key="d9">related_to</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-d9f905a36fae7e407107d1a11e7b7200</data>
  <data key="d11">Enapter_Datasheet_EL40_EN.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1792055476</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Enapter AEM Electrolyser EL 4.0 :: Production Rate" target="Enapter AEM Electrolyser EL 4.0 :: Heat Dissipation">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Production rate and heat dissipation together contribute to defining the unit’s operating envelope.</data>
  <data key="d9">related_to</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-d9f905a36fae7e407107d1a11e7b7200</data>
  <data key="d11">Enapter_Datasheet_EL40_EN.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1792055477</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Enapter AEM Electrolyser EL 4.0 :: Hydrogen Output Purity" target="Enapter AEM Electrolyser EL 4.0 :: Output Pressure">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Output pressure directly influences hydrogen purity: 35 barg gives 99.9% with &lt;1,000 ppm H₂O, whereas 8 barg gives 98.8% with &lt;12,000 ppm H₂O, while O₂ remains &lt;5 ppm in both cases.</data>
  <data key="d9">influences</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-d9f905a36fae7e407107d1a11e7b7200</data>
  <data key="d11">Enapter_Datasheet_EL40_EN.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1792055475</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Enapter AEM Electrolyser EL 4.0 :: Nominal Power Consumption per Nm³ of H₂ Produced" target="Enapter AEM Electrolyser EL 4.0 :: Operative Power Consumption">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The operative power of 2.4 kW is consistent with the nominal power consumption: 4.8 kWh/Nm³ × 0.5 Nm³/h (500 NL/h) = 2.4 kW.</data>
  <data key="d9">related_to</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-d9f905a36fae7e407107d1a11e7b7200</data>
  <data key="d11">Enapter_Datasheet_EL40_EN.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1792055477</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Enapter AEM Electrolyser EL 4.0 :: Operative Power Consumption" target="Enapter AEM Electrolyser EL 4.0 :: Peak Power Consumption">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Peak power is 3 kW, 25% above operative power.</data>
  <data key="d9">related_to</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-d9f905a36fae7e407107d1a11e7b7200</data>
  <data key="d11">Enapter_Datasheet_EL40_EN.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1792055478</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Enapter AEM Electrolyser EL 4.0 :: Operative Power Consumption" target="Enapter AEM Electrolyser EL 4.0 :: Standby Power Consumption">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Standby power is 0.3 kW, 12.5% of operative power.</data>
  <data key="d9">related_to</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-d9f905a36fae7e407107d1a11e7b7200</data>
  <data key="d11">Enapter_Datasheet_EL40_EN.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1792055478</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Enapter AEM Electrolyser EL 4.0 :: Heat Dissipation" target="Enapter AEM Electrolyser EL 4.0 :: Max Heat Dissipation">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Heat dissipation rises from 0.6 kW beginning of life to 0.9 kW end of life, showing degradation over the system lifetime.</data>
  <data key="d9">related_to</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-d9f905a36fae7e407107d1a11e7b7200</data>
  <data key="d11">Enapter_Datasheet_EL40_EN.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1792055478</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Enapter AEM Electrolyser EL 4.0 :: Maximum Water Input Conductivity" target="ASTM D1193-06 Type IV">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The maximum water input conductivity of the Enapter AEM Electrolyser EL 4.0 is minimum ASTM D1193-06 Type IV.</data>
  <data key="d9">conforms_to</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-d9f905a36fae7e407107d1a11e7b7200</data>
  <data key="d11">Enapter_Datasheet_EL40_EN.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1792055473</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Enapter AEM Electrolyser EL 4.0 :: Maximum Water Input Conductivity" target="ASTM D1193-06 Type II">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The maximum water input conductivity of the Enapter AEM Electrolyser EL 4.0 is recommended as ASTM D1193-06 Type II.</data>
  <data key="d9">conforms_to</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-d9f905a36fae7e407107d1a11e7b7200</data>
  <data key="d11">Enapter_Datasheet_EL40_EN.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1792055474</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Enapter AEM Electrolyser EL 4.0 :: Maximum Water Input Conductivity" target="ASTM D1193-06 Type III">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The maximum water input conductivity of the Enapter AEM Electrolyser EL 4.0 is recommended as ASTM D1193-06 Type III.</data>
  <data key="d9">conforms_to</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-d9f905a36fae7e407107d1a11e7b7200</data>
  <data key="d11">Enapter_Datasheet_EL40_EN.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1792055475</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Enapter AEM Electrolyser EL 4.0 :: Water Consumption" target="Water">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Water consumption specifies the amount of water consumed by the Enapter AEM Electrolyser EL 4.0.</data>
  <data key="d9">measures</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-d9f905a36fae7e407107d1a11e7b7200</data>
  <data key="d11">Enapter_Datasheet_EL40_EN.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1792055483</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Enapter AEM Electrolyser EL 4.0 :: Ambient Operative Humidity Range" target="Enapter AEM Electrolyser EL 4.0 :: IP Rating">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">IP 20 rating and ambient operative humidity range of up to 90% non-condensing describe installation and environmental constraints.</data>
  <data key="d9">related_to</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-d9f905a36fae7e407107d1a11e7b7200</data>
  <data key="d11">Enapter_Datasheet_EL40_EN.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1792055480</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Enapter AEM Electrolyser EL 4.0 :: Dimensions" target="Enapter AEM Electrolyser EL 4.0 :: Weight">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Dimensions, weight, 6 U cabinet space, IP 20 rating, and ambient ranges describe physical integration and installation constraints.</data>
  <data key="d9">related_to</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-d9f905a36fae7e407107d1a11e7b7200</data>
  <data key="d11">Enapter_Datasheet_EL40_EN.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1792055479</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Enapter AEM Electrolyser EL 4.0 :: Dimensions" target="Enapter AEM Electrolyser EL 4.0 :: Space Inside Cabinet">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Dimensions and 6 U cabinet space describe physical integration constraints for the Enapter AEM Electrolyser EL 4.0.</data>
  <data key="d9">related_to</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-d9f905a36fae7e407107d1a11e7b7200</data>
  <data key="d11">Enapter_Datasheet_EL40_EN.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1792055480</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
